 "title": "Parity decision trees on the sphere's count need polynomial depth",
 "subject": "The knot sphere's contradiction (the Kasteleyn-signed NAE formula of the octahedral sphere) in proof complexity",
 "conclusion": "Every parity decision tree that finds a violated line of the octahedral knot sphere, hence every tree-like Res(xor) refutation of its count, has depth at least c n^{1/8}/log n, because a shallow parity tree is a low-degree F2 refutation and the count needs F2 degree polynomial in n. Its size is at least 2 to its F2 polynomial-calculus degree minus 3.",
